---
description: Internationalization and editable texts
globs: "src/**/*.tsx,messages/*.json"
alwaysApply: false
---

- No hardcoded user-facing text in JSX, `aria-label`, `alt`, `title` or `placeholder`. Use `useTranslations('ns')` (client) or `await getTranslations('ns')` (server).
- Keys are grouped by screen/feature namespace (`contact.submit`), camelCase, describing meaning not wording.
- Add the key to every file in `messages/` in the same change (`pnpm check` fails on missing/extra keys).
- Interpolate with ICU (`"{count, plural, one {# item} other {# items}}"`), never string concatenation.
- Dates, numbers and currency via `useFormatter()` / `getFormatter()`.
- Components never import message files. Texts come from `loadMessages()` (`src/i18n/messages.ts`), which can be switched to a CMS/DB (`docs/recipes/remote-messages.md`).
- Intentional literals (brand mark, code sample): `{/* biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-hardcoded-jsx-text: <reason> */}` before the element (or `// biome-ignore-all ...` at the top of a file that cannot use translations, like `global-error.tsx`).
- The plugin cannot see strings inside expressions (`{cond ? 'Open' : 'Close'}`): translate those too.
